  "worked_solution": "First, we find the matrix $\\,P-\\lambda I:$\n\ufeff\ufeff\ufeff\n\n$$\nP-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}7-\\lambda  & 6 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4-\\lambda  & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3-\\lambda  & 11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(P-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nSince the determinant of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix is given by the product of the entries on the main diagonal, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}7-\\lambda  & 6 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4-\\lambda  & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3-\\lambda  & 11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (7-\\lambda )(-4-\\lambda )(3-\\lambda )(-5-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -7)(\\lambda +4)(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda +5) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$",
